  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $\u2016x\u2016=1.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $\u2016x\u2016=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,\u2016x\u2016=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $\u2016x\u2016=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,\u2016x\u2016=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,\u2016x\u2016=1}=5.\n$$",
